e list of received credential requests by their status.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-06-19\nVersion: 3.10\n\n--- Record 619 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support of the Additional Key Type Capability Invocation\nDescription: You can now use a new key type, Capability Invocation, which allows identities to generate tokens for securely sharing Verifiable Presentations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-06-19\nVersion: 3.10\n\n--- Record 620 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Discontinuation of Node 18 Jobs\nDescription: Jobs that use Node 18 build tool versions no longer work.  Action: Please upgrade your jobs to newer build tool versions. See Supported Tools.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deleted\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-18\nValid as Of: 2025-06-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n\",266\n109,\"--- Record 101 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Offboard data\nDescription: You can now use the Migration API to offboard data from the SAP Document Management service without causing data loss.  See Offboarding Data from SAP Document Management Service in the Multi-Cloud Foundation  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-09-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 102 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2025.19\nDescription: New and changed features are available for .  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2025.19. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-16\nValid as Of: 2025-09-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 103 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: SAP Document Management Service is supported as a repository type for the orchestration grounding module.  For more information, see Create a Generic Secret for AI Data Management.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-15\nValid as Of: 2025-09-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 104 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Access to Runtime Parameters\nDescription: Runtime Parameters has been removed from Quick Links. You can now access Runtime Parameters only through Component Monitor.See: Runtime Parameters\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 105 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Configure Istio Proxy Resources\nDescription: Manually increase resource limits for Istio Proxies for the worker component.See: Set Ixtio Proxy Resources\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 106 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Edge Local Authentication and Authorization Support for External Certificate Pinning.\nDescription: When pinning is disabled for external client certificates, the system doesn't accept a previously used certificate with an older issue date for authentication once you use a renewed certificate.  See: Edge Local Authentication and Authorization\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2506\n\n--- Record 107 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enabling ADK persistency with apadter API Available\nDescription: You can now utilize an adapter API to store and retrieve critical information ensuring data persistence even after node restarts or crashes.  See Enabling ADK Persistency\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 108 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Action in Job Management\nDescription: A new action, Consolidate MPL Aggregation Data, is available in Job Management.See: Job Management\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 109 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Reusable API Artifact\nDescription: You can now create reusable API artifacts that encapsulate standardized API policies and mediation logic such as authentication, transformation, and validation into modular units. These artifacts can be defined centrally and used across multiple API artifacts, helping you maintain consistency and streamline API development.   See, Reusable API Artifact  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 110 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: RFC Adapter Receiver Supported in Diagnostics\nDescription: The Adapter diagnostics task now also supports the RFC adapter with receiver direction.See: Diagnostics\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2507\n\n\",224\n429,\"--- Record 961 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enhancements to the Create Node dialog.\nDescription: When you create or edit a transport node, the destination selection box now displays both the name and description of each destination. The description makes it easier to choose the appropriate destination.  See:   Create Transport Nodes  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-06\nValid as Of: 2025-05-06\nVersion: 2504a\n\n--- Record 962 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New function in the import queue: Immediately start imports of transport requests as soon as they enter an import queue.\nDescription: This function enhances automation, and simplifies the import process.  See:   Enable Automatic Import  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-06\nValid as Of: 2025-05-06\nVersion: 2504a\n\n--- Record 963 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Revamp of the Landscape Action Logs\nDescription: The landscape action logs are now displayed in a more flexible table layout with extensive filter options, detail display, and links to the affected objects.   See:   Landscape Action Logs  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-06\nValid as Of: 2025-05-06\nVersion: 2504a\n\n--- Record 964 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: APIRule v2 upgrade and deletion of v1beta1 are postponed\nDescription:     After careful consideration, we have decided to postpone the release of API Gateway 3.0.0, which contains the APIRule v2 upgrade, to May 5, 2025.  Additionally, the planned deletion of v1beta1 for the end of May will also be postponed. A new target date will be announced in the future.  Required action: Migrate all your APIRule custom resources (CRs) to version v2.      To migrate your APIRule CRs from version v2alpha1 to version v2, you must update the version in APIRule CRs’ metadata.  To migrate your APIRule CRs from version v1beta1 to v2, follow the procedure described in the blog posts:   APIRule migration - noAuth and jwt handlers  APIRule migration - Ory Oathkeeper based OAuth2 handlers    For more information, see Changes Introduced in APIRule v2alpha1 and v2. Since the APIRule CRD v2alpha1 is identical to v2, the migration procedure from version v1beta1 to version v2 is the same as from version v1beta1 to version v2alpha1.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 965 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 3.0.2\nDescription: This version of the API Gateway module introduces APIRule CR in the stable version v2.   The new CRD allows you to expose your workloads using one of the three supported access strategies: jwt, noAuth, and extAuth. The noAuth access strategy provides a simple configuration for exposing workloads over the specified HTTP methods. The jwt access strategy allows you to secure your workload by defining Istio JWT configuration and the extAuth access strategy allows for providing custom authentication and authorization logic. For more information, see APIRule Custom Resource.  Additionally, version 3.0.2 contains the following fixes:  We've fixed the behavior of in-cluster connectivity when using JWT handler in APIRule. Now, in-cluster connectivity is blocked.  Now, when you create an APIRule with the noAuth access strategy, it is validated if the target workload has an Istio sidecar proxy injected.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-05\nValid as Of: 2025-05-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 966 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Assignees Column Available in Company Policies\nDescription: In the list of company policies (Configure  Data Spaces), the column Assignees now shows you how many clients are already assigned to the company policy.  See Create and Edit Company Policies.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-04\nValid as Of: 2025-05-04\nVersion: 2503\n\n--- Record 967 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription: The following are the latest versions in Data Space Integration:      Data Space Integration: 1.8.*      Increment: 2503      Tractus-X Eclipse Dataspace Connector: 0.7.6      FOSS Eclipse Dataspace Components: 0.7.2      See also the Release Notes of Catena-X. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-04\nValid as Of: \",209\n610,\"--- Record 781 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 3.0.4\nDescription: This release contains the following improvements:  We've unified extensibility views for APIGateway and APIRule custom resources in Busola.  Now, the order of rules in the APIRule custom resource is important. Rules defined earlier in the list have a higher priority than those defined later. For more information, see Significance of Rule Path Order.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-22\nValid as Of: 2025-05-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 782 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pricing - Access with Multiple Multi-Valued Attributes\nDescription: An access sequence that includ